Shader cache and shader/program robustness (Strikers a9c11e0)

From the Strikers port's vitaGL (custom_shaders.c, utils/shader_cache_io.h,
utils/shader_binary.h, utils/shader_candidate.h), without its GLB features
(pack lookup, read-only seed folder, stream arena flushes, table stats):
- cache entries are written whole to "<name>.tmp" and renamed into place; a
  failed or short write never leaves a truncated entry; an existing entry is
  replaced only by a complete new one (an entry that was rejected as invalid
  is rewritten instead of being recompiled on every start)
- cache reads are bounded (size checked, full read loop) and the entry is
  validated (GXP header, parameter table, matrix indices, sampler names,
  sceGxmProgramCheck) before it is registered; an invalid entry is ignored
  and the shader is compiled from source
- compile: the compiler's output size no longer overwrites the source length
  on failure; registration is the last step, so a failure leaves no
  registered half-built shader; optimised-out matrices are skipped
- link: handles, missing shaders, sampler/uniform resource indices and
  allocations are checked; a failed link restores the program as it was
  (PROG_UNLINKED, nothing leaked) instead of a half-linked program
- glDeleteProgram frees the default uniform buffers even when the program
  has no uniforms of that stage (they leaked before)
- glDeleteShader frees the compiler log in every case; attribute counts are
  bounded by VERTEX_ATTRIBS_NUM
The cache file format and names (%llX) are unchanged: existing caches stay
valid.
